From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: ROG5: the SM8350 root port is not hotpluggable

The SM8350 PCIe0 Root Port resets with Hot-Plug Capable and Hot-Plug
Surprise set in SLTCAP (lspci: SltCap HotPlug+ Surprise+), although the
WCN6855 behind it is soldered to the board. With CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE
off, pci_bridge_d3_possible() refuses D3 for such a port (is_pciehp and not
native), so the port stays in D0 in system suspend,
pci_host_common_d3cold_possible() returns false (kretprobe: ret=0 on every
s2idle), and dw_pcie_suspend_noirq() returns before PME_Turn_Off: the link,
the PCIe clocks (the aux clock is an XO consumer) and the interconnect votes
stay up, and qcom_stats cxsd/aosd never count.

Clear HPC and HPS in the 2.7.0 post_init (the path SM8350 uses), next to the
existing NCCS fixup.

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c	2026-09-27 13:23:14.981841153 +0200
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c	2026-09-27 13:23:14.994044533 +0200
@@ -377,6 +377,27 @@
 	dw_pcie_dbi_ro_wr_dis(pci);
 }
 
+/*
+ * ROG5: the SM8350 Root Port resets with Hot-Plug Capable/Surprise set in
+ * SLTCAP although the WCN6855 is soldered to the board. With the PCIe hotplug
+ * driver not built, pci_bridge_d3_possible() then refuses D3 for the port
+ * (pciehp not native), pci_host_common_d3cold_possible() fails, and
+ * dw_pcie_suspend_noirq() leaves the link, its clocks and interconnect votes
+ * up through every system suspend, so the SoC never reaches CX/XO shutdown.
+ * The slot is not hotpluggable: clear both bits.
+ */
+static void qcom_pcie_clear_slot_hotplug(struct dw_pcie *pci)
+{
+	u16 offset = dw_pcie_find_capability(pci, PCI_CAP_ID_EXP);
+	u32 val;
+
+	dw_pcie_dbi_ro_wr_en(pci);
+	val = readl(pci->dbi_base + offset + PCI_EXP_SLTCAP);
+	val &= ~(PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_HPC | PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_HPS);
+	writel(val, pci->dbi_base + offset + PCI_EXP_SLTCAP);
+	dw_pcie_dbi_ro_wr_dis(pci);
+}
+
 static void qcom_pcie_configure_dbi_base(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 {
 	struct dw_pcie *pci = pcie->pci;
@@ -1079,6 +1100,7 @@
 				pcie->parf + PARF_NO_SNOOP_OVERRIDE);
 
 	qcom_pcie_set_slot_nccs(pcie->pci);
+	qcom_pcie_clear_slot_hotplug(pcie->pci);
 
 	return 0;
 }
